====Usage notes====
Interjectional usage of {{m|fr||allez}} has gained significant distance, even disconnection and independence from the imperative form of {{m|fr|aller}} in which it originated. As such, while it retains a certain imperative thrust, the interjection is not affected by [[T-V distinction]] — that is to say, it may be directed toward someone whom the speaker would address with the familiar pronoun {{m|fr|tu}} or the deferential {{m|fr|vous}}. An especially clear demonstration of this phenomenon — arguably the clearest — can be observed in the phrase {{m|fr||allez vas-y}}, which appears to be composed of both plural/deferential and familiar singular second-person imperatives of {{m|fr|[[y aller|(y)]] [[aller]]}}, though the former is actually this now-independent interjection.


